Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["ExpandForms", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1110,ExpressionUUID->"be4bee5e-9886-4f8b-95d6-8759e5360cc8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"4fe48fbd-82ee-4ea4-8792-4e8db1410fc9"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["ExpandForms"]], 
     "paclet:VasilDimitrov/SolutionsX/ref/ExpandForms", 
     "VasilDimitrov Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["sol", "TI"], "]", "[", 
   StyleBox["expr", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "987fc183-fdd5-46a0-9186-99687e84810b"],
 "\[LineSeparator]rewrites every differential form of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["sol", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "cc47b246-0837-4547-ac14-45d7b5a90da5"],
 " appearing in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["expr", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "f20cb5df-ca4b-46de-a37d-aa74dd5c1684"],
 " as its companion tensor contracted with a wedge of coordinate \
differentials, and expands the exterior derivative of every degree-zero \
expression in the same sweep."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->1111,ExpressionUUID->"51dce3bc-71c2-4131-bede-c7029137ded6"],

Cell["\<\
ExpandForms[sol][expr] replaces each differential form of sol appearing in \
expr by its companion tensor contracted with a wedge of coordinate \
differentials, divided by the degree factorial.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1112,ExpressionUUID->"0d9e9629-90df-4f54-be12-d60efc5b8eb0"],

Cell["\<\
The companion tensor of a form named A is named TA, and is created \
automatically when the form is included.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1113,ExpressionUUID->"1f1725a3-01c8-44d0-a048-8676bc7a69ca"],

Cell["\<\
A form matches whatever indices it carries in expr: the replacement is \
generated from the index structure of the stored Symbol, not from the literal \
indices used at definition time.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1114,ExpressionUUID->"4c8d5127-6e3c-4bde-9aaa-822b6867a780"],

Cell["\<\
In the same sweep the exterior derivative of every degree-zero expression, \
such as a scalar or an already expanded companion tensor, is expanded as its \
covariant derivative contracted with a coordinate differential, so Diff[A[i]] \
expands fully without ExpandForms knowing any field-strength relation.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1115,ExpressionUUID->"bd6ea9ee-4186-464f-96f1-cd614a439948"],

Cell["\<\
Ambiguities resolve by the usual convention of taking the first: the exterior \
derivative expands on the first manifold, with the first metric's CovD.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1116,ExpressionUUID->"17462959-dba9-41e2-be94-5a5f946a6e58"],

Cell["\<\
This is the step that turns an equation written in form language into one \
that can be read off componentwise.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1117,ExpressionUUID->"7f8ce628-502b-486e-b8d0-e662c9fdd0a1"],

Cell["\<\
The contracted index is a generated dummy, so the result is usually read \
through ScreenDollarIndices.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1118,ExpressionUUID->"f689d402-1122-4a25-87c3-03f83dc77e19"],

Cell["ExpandForms has the attribute HoldFirst.", "Notes",
 CellID->1119,ExpressionUUID->"4e0dc3e5-fe9b-4e87-b448-878feb64165e"]
}, Open  ]],

